df - how much room is left

SYNOPSIS
    df [-h]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the size and free space of each mounted filesystem.

    Sizes are in 1K blocks, which is the form to do arithmetic on. -h prints
    them as KiB, MiB and GiB instead, which is the form to read.

    A filesystem that cannot answer - procfs has no blocks to count - is
    listed with dashes rather than left out, so that `df` and `mount` show the
    same set of names.

OPTIONS
    -h  sizes as KiB, MiB and GiB rather than as 1K blocks

SEE ALSO
    mount, du
